## Part D — In-depth Phase 4 implementation plan

This is the plan to hand your coding agent. **Phase 4's job: make every claim in your pitch deck true in the running code** — a backend that actually boots and is actually authenticated, an Eligibility Agent that actually evaluates rules, a Document Agent that actually reads real records, and a document upload that actually gets read by a vision model. Nothing here changes what the UI looks like; you're replacing the last remaining fake internals.

### D.1 Goals & definition of done

- The Render backend boots successfully from a clean deploy using either the Dockerfile or `render.yaml` (pick one, delete the other) — no `ModuleNotFoundError`.
- `POST /run` and `POST /extract-document` both reject any request missing a valid, exactly-matching `X-Sahayak-Internal-Secret` header, unconditionally — no "if present" gate, no hardcoded fallback value.
- `orchestrate-agent-run` rejects any request without a valid Supabase session — no citizen-impersonation fallback.
- `eligibility_agent_node` evaluates every rule against real data: numeric rules via a deterministic parser/comparator, qualitative rules via a real Groq call, and every evaluation writes a real `audit_logs` row citing the actual requirement text and the actual evidence value used.
- `document_agent_node` queries real `document_requirements` (for the selected scheme) and real `documents` (already on file for the citizen) and computes missing/verified sets from that — no hardcoded string, for any scheme.
- A citizen can upload a real file in `/documents`, have it land in Storage, and have a real Groq vision call (or its OCR fallback) populate `extracted_fields`/`confidence`/`status` on the `documents` row — no more constant "Rahul Sharma, DOB 15-08-2004" regardless of what was uploaded.
- The eligibility ↔ document loop closes for real: uploading the missing document and re-running actually reaches `application_agent` and a `COMPLETED` run. Today this path is structurally present in the graph but cannot be reached (Part 0, item 12/19) — after Phase 4 it must be reachable in a live demo.
- `seed-demo-data` produces the entire demo scenario in one call: schemes + rules + doc requirements (already there) **plus** the Rahul Sharma `profiles` row, **plus** an in-progress `applications` row, **plus** a `documents` row reflecting the missing enrollment certificate.
- `use-agent-run.ts` trusts `agent_runs.status` as ground truth (not agent-name string matching) and surfaces a visible error/retry state after a timeout instead of an infinite spinner.
- `/admin/agents` is fully real — the `MOCK_AGENT_EVENTS` simulation path is deleted, not just made to coexist with the real subscription.

